    LLM: 'Game: 6-Card Brag. Type: Partition/Vying. Rules: 6 cards dealt, split into 2 hands of 3. Brag rankings apply. Vying follows standard blind/see costs. Win both comparisons to claim pot.',
    Player: 'You have a pair of 3s, an Ace of Hearts, a 2 of Hearts, a 3 of Hearts, and a King. Do you put the 3s together for a winning pair, or split your cards to make a Flush in Hearts and a high-card King hand?',
    objective: 'Win the pot by having the highest-ranked hands across the partition or by forcing others to fold.',
    gameplay: '1. **Partition**: Players divide 6 cards into Hand A and Hand B. 2. **Vying**: Betting rounds proceed as in standard Brag. 3. **Comparison**: Showdown involves comparing corresponding hands. 4. **Ranks**: Prial > Running Flush > Run > Flush > Pair > High Card.',
    keyRules: [
      'Both three-card hands must be legal Brag combinations.',
      'In many variants, you must win both hand comparisons to take the entire pot; otherwise, it carries over.',
      'Blind betting applies to the entire 6-card set before viewing and partitioning.',
